Sutton [1988] made three assumptions to prove convergence of TDp0q to the optimal estimates:
1. sufﬁcient training data
2. repeated presentations of training data
3. the target system is linear
The author also showed that on multi-step prediction problems outperformed supervised learning. The family of TD
methods is denoted TDpλq, where 0 ¤ λ ¤ 1 is called the recency factor. Then, TDp0q is the difference between two
successive predictions, and TDpλq is the sum of TDp0q errors exponentially weighted by λ. In our previous example,
