6 for states B, C, D, E and F, respectively. Two experiments were set:
1. ∆w are accumulated over sequences and only used to update the weight vector after the complete presentation
of a training set. Each training set are presented repeatedly to each learning procedure until the latter no-longer
produce any signiﬁcant changes in the weight vector. This is the repeat presentations training paradigm.
