sequence is repeatedly presented (case r1s). One solution is to work backwards through the sequences. In the sequence
XD, XE, XF , 1, ﬁrst update the prediction for F in light of the 1, then the prediction for E is updated based on F, and
so on. Thus, the effect of 1 is back propagated to the start of the sequence with only a single presentation. However,
it no-longer has an incremental implementation. But if learning is done ofﬂine from an existing database, working
backward should produce the best predictions.
