16.2.6
Predicting cumulative outcomes
Rather that predicting the ﬁnal outcome z of a sequence, we can also predict cumulative outcomes. We assume that
each step of a sequence incur a cost, and want to predict, at time t, the expected total cost of the remaining sequence.
Here, the costs become known as the sequence evolves. We use the observation vector received at each step to predict
the total cumulative cost after that step. We want Pt to predict the remaining cumulative cost given the t-th observation.
We let ct 1 be the cost incurred between times t and t 1 and cij be the expected value of the cost incurred on transition
from state i to state j.
