φ : T  U  X Ñ Y
φ : t, u, xfwd Ñ ˆy  gpWoutr1}uptq}xfwdptqsq
ψ : T  Y  X Ñ U
ψ : t, y, xbwd Ñ ˆu  gpWrecr1}yptq}xbwdptqsq
xfwd : T  U  X  Y Ñ X
xfwd : t, u, x, y Ñ xfwdptq  fpWinuptq   Wresxpt  1q   Wfbˆypt  1qq
xbwd : T  U  X  Y Ñ X
xbwd : t, u, x, y Ñ xbwdptq  fpWinˆupt  1q   Wresxpt  1q   Wfbyptqq
(17.128)
Equations ( 17.128) above deﬁne the associative system. The system is now composed of two functions φ and ψ mapping respectively input to output and output to input. We have also deﬁned two states xfwd and xbwd corresponding
respectively to the states obtained with forward model φ and backward model ψ.
Remark 17.5 In practice the backward model cannot be use in our task (at least on the testing sample) as we obviously do not know the asset price we want to predict. However this framework demonstrates that we can compute its
corresponding input ˆu by simply using the last prediction ˆypt  1q.
