them is as large as possible. The region bounded by these two hyperplanes is called the margin, and the maximum
margin hyperplane is the hyperplane lying halfway between them. A linear classiﬁer can be considered as a hyperplane
with normal vector w P Rd and offset b. The classiﬁcation of xi is determined by the hyperplane:
