In learning, we want to minimise that objective function. Most of the algorithms are iterative in nature and will
hopefully converge to the optimal value. In order to ﬁnd the break-even point between the algorithms we want to
focus on the generalisation error, that is, the expected error on test set.
We can use online convex programming to optimise that problem, getting the Online SVM. Alternatively, we can
consider ofﬂine algorithm and apply the Lagrange multiplier or the kernel trick.
