The game is implemented by using an iterative, numerical approach. See Algorithm (26). First, the input noise z
is uniformly sampled, and then the mapping x  Gpzq imposes the non-uniform distribution pG on the transformed
samples. G contracts in regions of high density and expands in regions of low density. The gradient of D guides GpZq
to ﬂow to regions that are more likely to be classiﬁed as data. Eventually, if the pair pG, Dq has enough capacity, it
will reach a saddle point where DpXq  1
